### Phase 2: JavaScript Lazy Loading Implementation

#### 2.1 Source File Optimization

Transform JavaScript files by changing attributes:
- `type="text/javascript"` → `type="noscript-s"`
- `src="..."` → `data-src="..."`

**External Script Example:**
```liquid
<!-- Before -->
<script src="{{ 'shipping-note-script.js' | asset_url }}" type="text/javascript"></script>

<!-- After -->
{% if template contains 'index' or template contains 'product' or template contains 'collection' %}
  <script type="noscript-s" data-src="{{ 'shipping-note-script.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
{% else %}
  <script src="{{ 'shipping-note-script.js' | asset_url }}" type="text/javascript"></script>
{% endif %}
```

**Inline Script Example:**
```liquid
<!-- Before -->
<script>  
  $( document ).ready(function() {
    if(isBrave()){
      var braveImgShow = "{{ img_url }}";  
      $('.rimage-outer-wrapper .rimage-wrapper img').attr('src',braveImgShow);  
    }   
  });
</script>

<!-- After -->
<script {% if template contains 'index' or template contains 'product' or template contains 'collection' %}type="noscript-s"{% endif %}>  
  $( document ).ready(function() {
    if(isBrave()){
      var braveImgShow = "{{ img_url }}";  
      $('.rimage-outer-wrapper .rimage-wrapper img').attr('src',braveImgShow);  
    }   
  });
</script>
```

